# Advanced production analysis

Complete SCR-002's Production section with detailed distributions, a production-balance plot, and dice-reliance analysis.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Production is composed of distinct, vertically scrollable analysis elements.
- [x] Detailed production has `Cards per round` and `Rounds per card` modes with the specified help text.
- [x] All, Brick, Lumber, Ore, Grain, and Wool rows expand independently to aligned probability subrows.
- [x] Cards-per-round subrows show 0, 1, 2, 3, and 4+ card probabilities.
- [x] Rounds-per-card subrows show first production in 1, 2, 3, and 4+ rounds using the geometric distribution derived from `p0`.
- [x] Production contribution records include player, building ID/type, hex ID, resource, and dice number.
- [x] Settlements count once, cities twice, and per-round distributions support one through six active players.
- [x] All-resource means agree with summed resource means, while All distributions preserve same-roll resource correlations.
- [x] Production balance plots Brick, Lumber, Ore, Grain, and Wool clockwise and supports any subset of active players.
- [x] Production balance normalises every polygon against the maximum active-player/resource mean.
- [x] Dice reliance selects exactly one active player and toggles raw versus probability-weighted production.
- [x] Dice reliance displays dice results 2–12 excluding 7.
- [x] Production scrolling clamps at its limits and fixed/value table rows remain aligned.
- [x] Domain and UI regression coverage is added for changed behaviour.
- [x] App, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile.
- [ ] Live focused checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Implementation plan

1. Model production contributions and deterministic distributions.
2. Build the detailed expandable production table and help.
3. Add the radial production-balance plot and player multi-selection.
4. Add the dice-reliance selector, toggle, help, and chart.
5. Add tests, review the diff, and record verification evidence and remaining manual checks.

## Risks and clarifications

- Robber blocking is out of scope, but contribution records retain hex identity for future filtering.
- The All distribution is calculated from total production per dice outcome to retain correlations.
- The tab may scroll vertically to expose lower analysis elements.

